  "title": "Hemistitch · desktop prototype",
  "blurb": "One faux barrel drives the going train to a faux escapement; the motion works turn two compound discs, hours on the left and minutes on the right, read at a fixed index at 3 o’clock. Real size in mm: module 1 teeth in 2.8 mm acrylic layers, for the Makera Z1. Rods, bearings, plates and bridges come next. Lock what you place; ask Claude to check the rest.",
  "source": [
   "Numbers from the brief in VISION §10.8 (2026-11-10). Proportions: AXIS v1 grown 2.5× (case 50 × 29 mm, discs Ø19 at ±10.5 mm). Pinions carry +0.3 profile shift and wheels −0.3 so 12-leaf pinions aren’t undercut. The faux barrel stands in for the motor pod, which comes last."
  ],
